{"post_stream":{"posts":[{"id":493975,"name":"Mariusz Wójcik","username":"Mariusz_Wojcik","avatar_template":"/user_avatar/forum.cursor.com/mariusz_wojcik/{size}/121248_2.png","created_at":"2026-09-17T12:09:04.410Z","cooked":"\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-493975-where-does-the-bug-appear-featureproduct-1\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-493975-where-does-the-bug-appear-featureproduct-1\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eWhere does the bug appear (feature/product)?\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eGrok Bot\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-493975-describe-the-bug-2\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-493975-describe-the-bug-2\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eDescribe the Bug\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eToday all my defined bots  dissappeared. There were visible 14.09.2026 for sure. I finished the conversation due to limit this day. I used grok bot in both MacOS and my phone (Android). Everything worked fine till today.\u003cbr\u003e\nFirst I opened a MacOS app. I saw all my bots for a while, but then for some reason the list refreshed. Exact the same behaviour I noticed on mobile app.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eConfiguration took me a lot of time. I need them back.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-493975-steps-to-reproduce-3\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-493975-steps-to-reproduce-3\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eSteps to Reproduce\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eI do not now. I just opened the app.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-493975-expected-behavior-4\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-493975-expected-behavior-4\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eExpected Behavior\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eBots should not be auto removed for some reason.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-493975-screenshots-screen-recordings-5\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-493975-screenshots-screen-recordings-5\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eScreenshots / Screen Recordings\u003c/h3\u003e\